## Key Analytical Observations

<div style="border-left:4px solid #EF4444;background:#FEF2F2;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;">
<b>Underwriting deterioration:</b> The <span style="color:#EF4444;font-weight:600">Combined Ratio rose to 101%</span> from 92% in Q1FY24, driven primarily by the <span style="color:#EF4444;font-weight:600">Claims Ratio climbing to 67%</span> (from 56%), consistent with the accompanying chart trend for this period <doc_source>step7web3</doc_source>. A Combined Ratio above 100% signals the insurer is generating an <b>underwriting loss</b> — premiums alone no longer cover claims, expenses and commissions.
</div>

<div style="border-left:4px solid #F59E0B;background:#FFFBEB;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;">
<b>Solvency watch:</b> The <span style="color:#F59E0B;font-weight:600">Solvency Ratio of 1.64x</span> remains above the IRDAI regulatory floor of 1.50x but has declined from 1.80x in Q1FY24 — worth monitoring alongside the simultaneous underwriting loss.
</div>

<div style="border-left:4px solid #22C55E;background:#F0FDF4;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;">
<b>Balance-sheet strength:</b> <span style="color:#22C55E;font-weight:600">Net worth of ₹2,219.37 cr</span> and <span style="color:#22C55E;font-weight:600">Investments/AUM of ₹6,833.65 cr</span> are hard, audited statutory figures (NL-3, NL-12, NL-12A) — the company retains a solid capital and investment cushion despite the near-term claims pressure. Despite the underwriting strain, the bottom line remained <span style="color:#22C55E;font-weight:600">positive at ₹20.14 cr PAT</span>, likely aided by investment income offsetting the underwriting shortfall.
</div>

### Data-Integrity Notes

1. **No Q1FY25 Investor Presentation located**: Repeated web searches surfaced only peer decks (Star Health, Axis Bank, Capital Small Finance Bank) and Care Health's static disclosures landing page — never a company-specific Q1FY25 IP document <doc_source>step7web1</doc_source><doc_source>step7web2</doc_source><doc_source>step13web1</doc_source><doc_source>step14web1</doc_source>. Six deck-conventional metrics (Retail health GWP split, PAT-IFRS, Claims ratio-IFRS, Retail health market share, blended Investment yield) are left blank per the "no estimate" rule.
2. All figures are converted from ₹ Lakhs (as reported in the source PDF) to ₹ Crore by dividing by 10, consistent with the document's "Amount in Rs. Lakhs" convention.
3. Given the search-attempt cap and consistently negative results, deck-exclusive metrics could not be sourced in this session — if a Care Health Q1FY25 investor presentation exists on a restricted IR portal (e.g., a specific BSE/NSE corporate-announcement filing), it was not discoverable via public web search.</ans>
